 Clark  decided to hit the floors of toy trade  shows to get the word out about her  product still she found it difficult to  find people who shared her enthusiasm  finally however in your Clark was able  to convince a buyer from the right stuff  a high-end toy retailer to stock a few  trial copies of her video for their  stores when they sold out within three  days the right stuff agreed to sign an  exclusive deal with in your Clark baby  Einstein videos were now being  distributed in 34 stores across the  country and selling out fast  today the baby Einstein is being  produced by Disney and total revenues  are over 1  billion dollars annually  by tapping into a major frustration and  by helping other people solve it a new  Clarke was able to go from stay-at-home  mom to ultra successful entrepreneur to  help you take your company to the next  level here are three action items you  can learn from Julianne or Clarke  action item number one look for a need  some of the most successful businesses  in the world have been built around  solving personal frustrations if you're  looking to start a new business a great  place to start is to think about the  biggest frustrations that you've had in  your life and how you solved them if  it's big and painful enough chances are  other people have the same problems and  would pay you to solve it for them Anna  Clark had never been a videographer nor  had she had any previous interest in  starting our own company she was a  stay-at-home mom and it was a role she  loved she enjoyed spending time with her  newborn baby and was more than happy to  give up her full-time job to do so and  when it came to being a mother and her  Clark took her duties very seriously the  idea behind what would become a new  Clarks billion-dollar baby was born from  a need a simple need that had been right  under her nose she wanted a learning  tool for a new child and when she  couldn't find what you wanted on the  market she decided to create her own  inner Clark stuck to what she knew best  babies she didn't spend countless hours  in search of a business idea the  business idea found her and it was  because a new Clark had kept her eyes  open to such an opportunity that she was  able to seize it when it came along  according to a new Clark believe it or  not when I stopped working when I was  six months pregnant I had no intention  of going back to work when my daughter  was born I started taking her to museums  and places like that but it wasn't very  engaging to her or to me I knew my baby  I knew what she liked to look at I  assumed that what my baby like to look  at most other babies would too the first  Baby Einstein video took off because it  was completely new concept it was an  entirely new idea no one else had done  videos for babies  action memo number two spread the word  you can have the greatest product or  service in the world but it won't take  off unless you tell people about it make  sure the value that you provide is so  incredible that people can't help but  talk about you to their friends and  family word-of-mouth marketing is highly  effective and extremely cheap but you  have to give them something to talk  about so just how exactly did her  basement operation become the billion  dollar industry leader that it is today  what it all came down to she says was  her ability to hit the streets and get  people talking about her business when  the first Baby Einstein video came out a  new Clark could not find any takers for  it took a more than a year to come up  with an idea on how to do that but  finally a new Clark knew what she had to  do she packed up and headed to New York  City for the American International Toy  Fair she was determined to get one of  the buyers from the right start a  high-end bebe retailer to take notice of  her video after that the man for Baby  Einstein products exploded according to  a new Clark I knew if I could get it  into the hands of a mom or an executive  who had a baby that would sell it I ran  up to them and said you're going to love  this video you have to watch it it's  perfect for your store there was a  reporter from People magazine who loved  it and wrote a piece on it  there was a producer on Oprah that also  loved it and they put it into a segment  parenting magazine also named Baby  Einstein video of the year at the end of  the day word of mouth is your most  important means to get the word out and  we have a great group mothers  number three build a brand when you're  creating your business pay close  attention to your messaging and how you  want the world to know you if you can  articulate your message in a clear and  unique way it not only helps people  understand what is that you do and if  it's for them it also helps them tell  other people as well if people can't  remember what you do and why you're  special they can't tell their friends  about you what parent wouldn't want  their kids who grew up to be the next  Albert Einstein for the company's name  to the rest of its promotional strategy  in your clark created and implemented a  brilliant branding strategy that helped  her innovative concept achieve the  success that it did Einstein might not  have watched playful videos with puppets  as a child but that hasn't stopped  thousands of parents and buying the Baby  Einstein series in the hopes that the  videos will aid in the development of  their children  none of the company's promotional  literature was ever still bold as to  claim that their products were  specifically engineered to make babies  smarter but with a name like Baby  Einstein the powers of association leave  little up the chance a new Clark was  saying the things parents wanted to hear  and making a product's parents thought  the kids needed to see and some circles  any parent who was not showing their  kids be behind some videos was even seen  as a bad parent that was a true mark of  success of a new Clarks branding  strategy according to a